Bottom composition data from the U.S. Geological Survey (fetch-seabed), licence gate
(spec 6.10), metadata read 2026-10-29. Each passes as a US Government work in the public domain:

  usSEABED Pacific Coast, Data Series 182 (doi:10.3133/ds182), pac_ext and pac_prs:
    Access_Constraints: None
    Use_Constraints: "Public domain data from the U.S. Government are freely redistributable
    with proper metadata and source attribution. Please recognize the U.S. Geological Survey
    (USGS) as the source of this information."
  CMECS Admiralty Inlet, Open-File Report 2015-1073 (doi:10.3133/ofr20151073), Data Series 935:
    Access_Constraints: None
    Use_Constraints (excerpt): "This information is not intended for navigational purposes.
    [...] Acknowledge the U.S. Geological Survey in products derived from these data. Share
    data products developed using these data with the U.S. Geological Survey. This database
    has been approved for release and publication by the Director of the USGS. [...]"
    The report itself states: "Although this report is in the public domain, permission must
    be secured from the individual copyright owners to reproduce any copyrighted material
    contained within this report." No copyrighted material is named for the GIS data.
  CMECS offshore Seattle (doi:10.5066/P9GVRZ3M), offshore Tacoma (doi:10.5066/P9KA6GH2),
  offshore Burien (doi:10.5066/P96T1B44), Data Series 935:
    Access_Constraints: None
    Use_Constraints: "USGS-authored or produced data and information are in the public domain
    from the U.S. Government and are freely redistributable with proper metadata and source
    attribution. Please recognize and acknowledge the U.S. Geological Survey as the originator
    of the dataset and in products derived from these data."
  Each charts pack NOTICE that holds USGS features names these sources.

Geoid grids (build-bathy fetches them from https://cdn.proj.org/ into the cache; used to convert CRM
EGM2008 heights to NAVD88, never shipped in a pack). License read 2026-11-09 in the PROJ-data
READMEs (https://github.com/OSGeo/PROJ-data, us_nga/us_nga_README.txt and us_noaa/us_noaa_README.txt):

  us_nga_egm08_25.tif   EGM2008 geoid model, US National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA),
                        2.5 minute grid produced with GeographicLib. License: Public Domain
  us_noaa_g2018u0.tif   GEOID18, US National Geodetic Survey (NOAA NGS), conterminous US,
                        NAD83(2011) to NAVD88. License: Public Domain

Tide station datums (regions/datum/wa-stations.toml) are from the NOAA CO-OPS datums API, a US
Government work.

Bundled fonts (fonts/, used to render glyph ranges):

  Noto Sans v2.015 (Regular, Bold)  SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL.txt)
    Static hinted TTFs from the notofonts/latin-greek-cyrillic release NotoSans-v2.015.

Symbols (symbols/*.svg) are drawn in-house after US Chart No. 1 (public domain).
